mb|2D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|2@D is reasonable but I would open 3@D with a 7-card suit. Some players will downgrade a weak 7-card suit and open a weak2 rather than preempting at the 3 level. As a |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lott,Law of Total Tricks^*N|CP||FP||at| advocate, I almost always use suit length to determine the level of my preempts. In addition, on this hand, 7-4-1-1 is especially attractive so I definitely prefer opening 3@D to 2@D.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 1 ***** |


mb|2N|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|East bid is fine. That is how preempt forces opponents to make uncomfortable bids. 2NT bid means strong NT with diamond stopper.|
PG| ***** 2 ***** |


mb|P|mb|3C|mb|P|mb|3S|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|P|mb|3N|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|West's auction was very reasonable. though, I would be worried about making 6@C. However, the only choice to get to 6@C is to bid 4@C |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=gerberetc,Gerber^*N|CP||FP||at|.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 3 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|And if partner shows two aces, hope that one is the @HA or if the @SA then partner has the @HK. 

        3@C by West was |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=stayman,Stayman^*N|CP||FP||at|.|

