mb|?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|There is a fairly complicated convention that you can use when the opponents make a 2 suited bid when both suits are known. In particular when they bid an unusual 2N (which shows the 2 lower unbid suits) or they make a minor suited |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=michaels,Michaels^*N|CP||FP||at| bid (which shows hearts and spades).|
PG| ***** 62 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|It does not apply when they make a major suit |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=michaels,Michaels^*N|CP||FP||at| bid, because only one suit is known (the other major).|
PG| ***** 63 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|It is called "unusual over unusual" although I don't particularly like the name. A double by me here says I am willing to penalize at least one of their 2 suits.|
pg| ***** 64 ***** |


mb|D|mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I would bid 2@S with the West hand, although pass is not out of the question.|
pg| ***** 65 ***** |


mb|P|mb|2H?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Now I am going to pass which is forcing since I made the double. My pass means I was willing to penalize spades. North, my partner, must do something, either double or bid clubs. However, double is reasonable, although not sure how well it will work here. He could also bid 2N since I said I had spades.|
PG| ***** 66 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BEast: ^*NHow does North know you have spades, because you passed my heart bid?|
PG| ***** 67 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I doubled saying I could penalize at least one of your suits and since I didn't double 2@H that means I could have double 2@S.|
